    <tr><td>2 · Import → freeze</td><td><strong>Normalize</strong> every source into one source-agnostic in-code artifact + provenance, <strong>and archive the raw native payload</strong> (opaque, non-canonical) for lossless offline re-normalization; Figma is an importer that pins <code>?version</code> and freezes the bytes</td><td>Freeze-to-in-repo consensus · ephemeral CDN URLs force byte-download · single-substrate contract avoids per-source lock-in · re-fetch from Figma is unreliable (versions can be dropped)</td></tr>
